{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"frouzy-brattish-muskrat","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\n10 modules directly under `tests/scripts/` have a `<name>_heldout.py` twin. Once both oracles have been reviewed the split only doubles module count, duplicates identical helper definitions, and makes every rename touch two files. Across these 10 pairs no test-function name collides; 7 pairs carry helper/fixture/class/const definitions with differing bodies (this directory has the densest rename set) and every other colliding definition is identical. Three of the held-out twins — `test_check_adr_numbers_heldout.py`, `test_check_config_ownership_heldout.py`, `test_check_config_reads_heldout.py` — lose their real-tree and CI-wiring tests in the test-suite epic's single-owner story (E10a-S3, aware-obvious-sphinx); this story merges the post-E10a-S3 remainder of those three modules. The pair list with per-pair rename sets, filtered from enumeration (2) of the test-suite epic's first comment, is itemised in this ticket's first comment. Cites are on origin/main 083620b0.\n\n## Approach\nDirectory: `tests/scripts/` — 10 pairs, 7 renames (`test_backfill_bug_class`, `test_backfill_complexity_clone`, `test_canary_bridge`, `test_check_adr_numbers`, `test_check_config_ownership`, `test_check_config_reads`, `test_normalize_ci_conclusion_port`). For each pair: `cat` the held-out module into the base under a `# ── held-out oracles (merged from <name>_heldout.py) ──` divider; keep the base module docstring and append the held-out docstring's \"what it proves\" paragraph; dedupe identical definitions (`pytestmark` counts here — keep the base copy); rename differing definitions and repoint their callers; `git rm` the held-out file. Rename rule: suffix the HELD-OUT definition `_heldout` (e.g. `_load_heldout`, `_SCRIPT_HELDOUT` for a constant, `gate_heldout` for a fixture) and repoint its callers; keep the base copy of identical definitions. `tests/scripts/test_check_config_reads_red_proof.py` (the only `*_red_proof.py`) is untouched and stays a separate module; `tests/scripts/test_check_config_reads.py` and its twin cite bug 2c58-e710-275e-4ff7, and that docstring stays the base docstring. No test body changes.\n\n## Scope\nIn scope: the 10 base modules under `tests/scripts/` named in the first comment and their 10 `_heldout` twins. Out of scope: `tests/scripts/test_check_config_reads_red_proof.py`, the 4 unpaired `tests/scripts/` held-out modules (renamed in S5), the pairs of S1, S2 and S3, every `scripts/check_*.py`, the `Makefile`, every file under `src/`, and any test body change.\n\n## Testing\nPer pair: `pytest --collect-only -q <base> <heldout>` before and `pytest --collect-only -q <base>` after — counts equal (both recorded on this ticket; the before count for the three `test_check_*` pairs is taken after E10a-S3 landed); `pytest <base>` green. `make test` green.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Zero paired twins remain in this directory: for each of the 10 pairs `git ls-files tests/scripts/<base>_heldout.py` prints nothing (the 4 unpaired `_heldout` modules here are untouched and renamed in S5).\n- [ ] Per-pair node counts reconcile: each merged base collects exactly the sum of the two prior counts, from the before/after `pytest --collect-only -q` runs recorded on this ticket.\n- [ ] `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` shows `new=0` (no `tests/_*.py` helper, check script, workflow step, nor autouse fixture is added).\n- [ ] `make verify` green.","id":"7a7a-ceb9-e9a5-4d8e","parent_id":"6ed2-24e5-6985-4faa","priority":2,"tags":["complexity-reduction","breaking-pass-4"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Merge the 10 held-out twin test pairs under tests/scripts"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788807297274285950,"uuid":"8227ac54-9f5a-4c94-812d-31b51f4da770"}